{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:1.1-3", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-3"}, "paraphrase": "One should meditate on the 'point of light' (tejobindu), subtle and beyond the senses, hard to see and reach; it is for the one who has conquered food, anger, association, the senses and the pairs of opposites.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ultimate", "practice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:1.15-16", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.15-16"}, "paraphrase": "The limbs are fifteen: yama, niyama, tyāga, mauna, deśa, kāla, āsana, mūlabandha, dehasāmya, dṛksthiti, prāṇasaṃyamana, pratyāhāra, dhāraṇā, ātmadhyāna and samādhi.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:tejobindu-fifteen-limbs"], "concepts": ["cpt:jnana-limbs"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:1.17-32", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.17-32"}, "paraphrase": "Each limb is knowledge: yama is restraint of the senses by the knowledge 'all is Brahman'; niyama the flow of like thoughts; silence is not mere silence of speech (that is for children); the true seat is where Brahman-contemplation flows; the true root-lock is Brahman, root of the worlds; evenness of body is dissolving in the even Brahman, not the straightness of a dry tree; the true gaze is seeing the world as Brahman, not looking at the nose-tip; prāṇāyāma is stopping all modifications by seeing all as Brahman — negating the world is exhalation, 'I am Brahman' inhalation, steadiness retention.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:jnana-limbs"], "practices": ["prc:jnana-pranayama"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:1.33", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.33"}, "paraphrase": "This (inner prāṇāyāma) is for the awakened; pressing the nose is for the ignorant.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:jnana-limbs"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:1.40-41", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.40-41"}, "paraphrase": "In practising samādhi obstacles arise: lack of inquiry, sloth, desire for enjoyment, dissolution (laya), darkness, distraction, radiance (tejas), sweating and blankness; the knower of Brahman should avoid them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "powers-experiences"], "obstacles": ["obs:tejobindu-samadhi-vighnas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:1.42-47", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.42-47"}, "paraphrase": "By thinking of an existent one becomes it, by thinking of the void, void; by the thought of Brahman, fullness; those who merely talk of Brahman without that inner state, attached to pleasure, are born again and again.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:2-akhandaikarasa", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2 (akhaṇḍaikarasa)"}, "paraphrase": "Kumāra asks Śiva about the partless, single-flavoured pure consciousness; Śiva teaches that everything — self, world, teacher, scripture — is that consciousness alone.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:siva"], "speaker": "Śiva", "addressee": "Kumāra", "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:4-jivanmukta-and-videhamukta", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4 (jīvanmukta and videhamukta)"}, "paraphrase": "Kumāra asks about the one liberated in life and the one liberated without body: the jīvanmukta abides as pure consciousness, free of 'I' and 'mine', while the body continues; the videhamukta is Brahman without remainder.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti", "cpt:videhamukti"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tejobindu-upanisad:5-atma-anatma-viveka", "source": "src:tejobindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5 (ātma-anātma-viveka)"}, "paraphrase": "Nidāgha asks Ṛbhu to teach discrimination of self and not-self; Ṛbhu teaches that the Self is beyond the three states, bodies and sheaths, and all else is not-self and unreal.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "body-layers"], "teachers": ["tch:rbhu", "tch:nidagha"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
